To force a text field in Adobe's Flash (ActionScript) to display columns, you can use the `TextField` class along with a `TextFormat` object to set the desired column width. Here's a simple example:

```actionscript
import flash.text.TextField;
import flash.text.TextFormat;

var myTextField:TextField = new TextField();
var myTextFormat:TextFormat = new TextFormat();
myTextFormat.columnWidth = 100; // Set the column width to 100 pixels

myTextField.defaultTextFormat = myTextFormat;
myTextField.text = "This is some sample text that will be displayed in columns.";
myTextField.width = 400; // Set the width of the text field

addChild(myTextField);
```

In this example, we create a `TextField` and a `TextFormat` object. We set the `columnWidth` property of the `TextFormat` to 100 pixels, which will force the text to be displayed in columns with a width of 100 pixels. We then apply this text format to the text field and set its width to 400 pixels. Finally, we add the text field to the display list.

You can adjust the `columnWidth` and `width` properties to fit your specific needs.

